-</tool>
+# Outputs
+
+Depending on the selection under *Additional output format* the tool produces:
+
+- **BED** — one interval per detected CRISPR array, in zero-based, half-open
+  coordinates as required by the BED format
+- **Tabular** — one row per repeat/spacer unit with the repeat position, the repeat
+  and spacer sequences and their lengths
+- **GFF (summary / detailed)** — `repeat_region` features, or additionally the
+  individual `repeat_unit` features when the detailed variant is selected
+- **Spacer sequences** — the extracted spacers as FASTA
+
+-----
 
+# Notes
+
+- For raw short reads (100-200 bp) use
+  [Crass](https://github.com/ctskennerton/Crass) instead.
+- Since minced 0.3.2 repeats that touch the edge of a contig are discarded, so a
+  partial repeat or spacer at the very end of a sequence may be lost.
+
+]]></help>
+    <expand macro="citations"/>
+</tool>
